        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "Subgrid turbulent mixing"
      },
      {
        "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 11501,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 503,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 169,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "In the surf zone large amounts of turbulence are generated due to wave breaking. To account for the exchange of momentum due to the unresolved scales on the grid a Smagorinsky-type sub grid model (Smagorinsky, 1963) is used. Formally such a sub-grid model is achieved after filtering the small scale motions out of the governing equations by filtering them over a volume of one or several grid-cells. The resulting equations apply to the large scale motions of the flow. In this context the sub-grid stress can be formulated as"
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 11568,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 505,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 171,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "Where  represents the stress and  the eddy viscosity. This eddy viscosity is expressed in terms of flow properties on the resolved scale as"
      },
      {
        "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
